From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey <sergey@local>
Date: Sun, 31 May 2026 03:31:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Treat Yandex no_data devices as available

Yandex IoT can return `state: no_data` for devices that still have valid
capability/property state, for example an AC reporting on/off, target
temperature, current temperature, and modes. Initial entity creation treats
all states except `offline` as available, but update handling only accepted
`online` and `unknown`, causing the entity to become unavailable on the first
cloud refresh.

Keep update availability consistent with initial availability: only
`offline` means unavailable.
---
 custom_components/yandex_station/core/entity.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/custom_components/yandex_station/core/entity.py b/custom_components/yandex_station/core/entity.py
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/custom_components/yandex_station/core/entity.py
+++ b/custom_components/yandex_station/core/entity.py
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@ class YandexEntity(Entity):
         self.quasar.subscribe_update(device["id"], self.on_update)
 
     def on_update(self, device: dict):
-        self._attr_available = device["state"] in ("online", "unknown")
+        self._attr_available = device.get("state") != "offline"
 
         self.internal_update(
             extract_state(device["capabilities"]) if "capabilities" in device else {},
-- 
